{"baseRefName":"codex/round111-seed-block-confirmation","body":"**BLOCKED. ENS-C: INCOMPLETE_ATTRIBUTION. M-B: INCOMPLETE_ATTRIBUTION.**\nThe fixed 20-arm experiment has 12 qualified completions, one interrupted arm and seven unstarted arms. All 30 pair positions remain: 18 evaluable and 12 UNEVALUABLE. Cold P-GRB remains the primary benchmark.\n\nCold-P comparisons combine startup and exact-backend differences. This change adds a default-off research control, P-S, that independently pays for the unchanged current 24+1 ENS startup H, physically verifies its own complete fleet, and submits one complete, externally checked and natively read-back Start to the true original compact model. Its matrix, variable types, bounds, objective, exhaustive-block policy, solver parameters and absolute work deadline remain unchanged. P-S retains its own lawful startup UB; it imports no cross-arm Start, UB, bound or cache. E/P-S and B/P-S compare complete backend combinations, including handoff and search interactions. They do not isolate AM or identify additive percentages. P-S/P measures the net effect of the independently paid startup and handoff. P-S is neither a new mathematical algorithm nor a default replacement.\n\nThe five predeclared roles cover positive-objective proof/discovery (F2), the distinct C2 repair, historical multi-leaf exposure (L48), proved-zero completion cost (G50-C1), and an unproved-zero V100 own-UB tradeoff (G100-R2). Each backend retains denominator five and vector **WIN / WIN / LOSS / UNEVALUABLE / UNEVALUABLE**, with three eligible roles out of five.\n\n| Completed role | ENS/P | M-B/P | P-S/P | ENS/P-S | M-B/P-S | M-B/ENS |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F2 | WIN | WIN | LOSS | WIN | WIN | LOSS |\n| R98-C2 | severe LOSS | WIN | severe LOSS | WIN | WIN | WIN |\n| R108-L48 | WIN | WIN | WIN | LOSS | LOSS | TIE |\n\nAll six completed backend/P-S comparisons match the full 25-seed semantic H traces, accepted actions, complete fleets with actual vehicle capacity assignments, and inventories, with actual backend exposure. At F2, ENS/M-B certify positive F approximately 0.865943520323 while P/P-S remain open. Cold P already found that target early, so its remaining difference is a proof tail. M-B's C2 own-U/gap improvement survives the P-S control. At L48, all three warm methods certify positive F approximately 0.201708522994, but P-S's whole time of 1285.0358 s is faster than ENS's 1552.9688 s and M-B's 1585.4304 s. Both X/P-S losses are nonsevere. Actual parent splits are zero at F2/C2 and two per tailored method at L48. Speculative child LPs do not become actual splits, and these observations do not identify AM causality.\n\nArm 13, G50-C1 M-B, was interrupted when the frozen wrapper's atomic status-file replacement raised Windows WinError5. Its finally block killed and waited for the active child; no optimizer remained. Concurrent Get-Content monitoring is a possible sharing conflict, with no proven unique cause. The arm lacks final output, an observer journal, the necessary audit and a whole clock. Its partial own physical F approximately 0.008182628, three returned LP calls and an unreturned terminal MIP remain separate observations, never a formal endpoint. Under the frozen once-only contract, no arm is retried, no performance helper is patched, and arms 14-20 stay unstarted. Missing geography is not recorded as an algorithm failure or TIE.\n\nValidation includes eight fresh original reference models (zero Optimize), H100 four-method cap-120 CLIs, positive-5/24 P/P-S and own-zero P-S micros, finite production full-Start valid/fault cases, independent pre-arm ACCEPT, and actual positive/negative postformal and final-reader reviews. All methods use measured production source `d0014a7163e3996fe120471420e56b089c9715ae` and PE `a8356b6ad6a5ced47e0d41374ec2184669349c083370eabd76989fb9c11539a8`. The 206 source and 38 performance-helper bindings remain frozen. Original signed-gap, 1e-7 numerical certification, complete-clock and materiality policies remain. Tiny negative gaps, null/error fields, severe costs and all failed fees are retained. Correct submission, read-back, observed incumbent evidence and hidden native search causality are distinguished.\n\nActual closed charge: **39 conservative starts / 18061.35593342781 outer seconds upper**, including qualification's 19 starts / 698.0634860992432 s, within the total 56/48000 and qualification 20/1800 limits. Failed declared slots are not refunded; nested native time is not added again.\n\nThe current-only 82,842,777-byte carrier binds 55,916 files. It excludes PE/DLL/license/credentials and old full carriers and stays below 95 MiB without artificial splitting. Actual public export and fresh empty-root restoration succeeded. One raw reconstruction from the restored root reproduced all 39 core files byte-for-byte; subsequent comparison passed 619,641 CSV fields and both JSON files. The initial combined comparison hit the standard CSV field-size limit. Only a separate stdlib comparison process's field capacity was increased, with error receipts retained and no reader change, raw rebuild, repack or native rerun. Independent restored-root review passed using public/restored/rebuilt roots only. The historical admission's offline-reader binding is explicitly superseded by the independently reviewed final offline reader; production and performance-helper bindings remain unchanged. Actual recovery receipts are recorded separately after scientific payload commit `a3cac1df0ee1d4eaaeb87343508e0af31cfc3b40`.\n\nR111 stays CONFIRMATION_SUPPORT / R110_MAIN_36_PLUS_R111_SEED_6. R110 stays BLOCKED at old arm 42's whole-cap excess. This finite exposed-role panel is not new independent confirmation, population significance, a paper benchmark or an adoption gate. ENS remains the default; no stopped mechanism is reopened and no winners are spliced across roles. The single next conditional priority is a separately frozen complete attribution experiment, preceded by finite validation of the implicated Windows sharing/atomic-status contract. This round ends with its BLOCKED delivery and does not automatically start that work.\n","headRefName":"codex/round112-paid-start-backend-attribution","headRefOid":"1e90dbc5eacddedf925d88c8608e897c56b4ad69","headRepository":{"id":"R_kgDOS_nLtA","name":"TailoredExact","nameWithOwner":"yifanXovo/TailoredExact"},"headRepositoryOwner":{"id":"U_kgDOCjxi3Q","login":"yifanXovo"},"isDraft":true,"number":174,"state":"OPEN","title":"Round112: test tailored backend contribution against a self-paid ENS-start compact control","url":"https://github.com/yifanXovo/TailoredExact/pull/174"}
